From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:45:39 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Give the ribbon's wall refusal its numbers

"The ribbon's cavity reached the domain wall; the volume must be interior,
with clearance to spare" did not say how much clearance was missing. The two
ribbon sites in _place_thin_volume_2d now raise _wall_refusal_2d, which gives:
the wall vertex the cavity touched, how far the cavity reaches from the band's
skin, how far the nearest wall vertex is from it, and the two terms of the
carve's reach there (clearance x h and 0.6 x width). It names the move that
would clear the wall, and the lever, chosen by whichever term governs. The
check itself (#549, #670) is unchanged, and "reached the domain wall" stays,
because the campaign drivers retry on it.

test_0865 places an interior ribbon 0.1 from the outer wall of an annulus with
cells of 0.05. It fails on the old message; on this one it reads
reach 0.112 and nearest wall vertex 0.0335.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
